"profiles": {
"Black Loops": "Black Loops is an electronic DJ and producer known for his deep house and house music sets. He primarily operates in Berlin and has performed at various clubs and festivals in Europe, including H\u00d6R, Hush Hush, and Bass Coast. His music is also featured on labels like Toy Tonics and Gruuv.\nPerforms as: Black Loops\nTheir channels, stations, shows, clubs, labels, collaborators: H\u00d6R BERLIN; Keep Hush; Balamii; F\u00eate; Music is 4 Lovers; Djoon; Bangkok Community Radio; Paradiso Pop-Up Club; Sisyphos; Watergate; Standard Time Toronto; Toy Tonics; Gruuv; LINEA; Neovinyl Recordings; Shall Not Fade; It's Deep; Ben Gomori / Turned On; Kono Vidovic; Rinse FM; Shadow Child; Data Transmission Radio; Sunshine 101 Radio Media; Gomma; Gabu Records; eZo; QUERICO TOKYO; Parkett; Goutier; Buongiorno Classic\nOther people with the name (not this artist): Black Loops (Toy Tonics / Gruuv, It) - This Black Loops is associated with the Toy Tonics and Gruuv labels, based in Berlin, Germany.; Black Loops (Deep Town Jozi) - This Black Loops is based in Johannesburg, South Africa, and is known for his deep house sets.",
"Desert Sound Colony": "Desert Sound Colony is an electronic DJ and producer known for their deep house and tech house sounds. They are based in London and are associated with the UK electronic music scene, collaborating with various DJs and producers and performing at notable clubs and festivals.\nPerforms as: Desert Sound Colony\nTheir channels, stations, shows, clubs, labels, collaborators: Holding Hands Records; PIRATE.COM; Bloop London Radio; Junction 2 Festival; LINEA; CDR; THUMP; Codex Natur\u00e6; Greg May; Adam Pits; Baby Roll\u00e9n; Rinse FM; DTRH; FH; Touching Bases; Le Protocole Radio; Slack's; Casino Times; Pressure Dome; Mr. Redley\nOther people with the name (not this artist): Desert Sound Colony (musician) - Based in London, known for their deep house and tech house sounds, active in the UK electronic music scene.; Desert Sound Colony (podcaster) - Not related to the musician, this name is used for a podcast channel.",
"Gene on Earth": "Gene On Earth is an electronic DJ and producer known for his deep house and tech house sounds. He is active in the electronic music scene, performing at various clubs and festivals, and collaborating with other notable DJs and producers. Gene On Earth is based in Europe, particularly in cities like Brussels and Amsterdam.\nPerforms as: Gene on Earth\nTheir channels, stations, shows, clubs, labels, collaborators: The Lot Radio; themuddshow; Dimensions Festival; Oli Burns; Club Space Miami; Love International Festival; Fuse Brussels; After Caposile; Wildeburg; dekmantel; Gray Area; Dimensions Festival; OBSESSION RADIOSHOW; Boiler Room; MAHAR; Resident Advisor; VBX; Wildeburg; Club Chinois; ECLUD\nOther people with the name (not this artist): Gene On Earth (producer) - Based in the Netherlands, known for his tech house and deep house productions.; Gene On Earth (DJ) - Based in Belgium, known for his live DJ sets and collaborations with other DJs.",
"Pierre Marty": "Pierre Marty is an electronic DJ and producer known for his live sets and performances. He is associated with the Enclave rooftop series in Rome and has been featured on channels like Esprit Occitanie and Curious?. His music is primarily electronic and he is active in the electronic music scene, particularly in Rome and other parts of Italy.\nPerforms as: Pierre Marty\nTheir channels, stations, shows, clubs, labels, collaborators: Enclave Rooftop Series; Rooftop Set in Rome; Esprit Occitanie; Curious?; Curiosity Freestyle 2 (LIVE ACT)\nOther people with the name (not this artist): Jean Pierre Marty (1981 performance) - This is a different person, a pianist who performed in 1981 with the Orchestra Scarlatti Rai.; Pierre Marty (TV5MONDE) - This is likely a different person, possibly a news anchor or presenter for TV5MONDE.",
"Van Bellen": "Joost van Bellen is a Dutch electronic DJ and producer known for his work in house and trance music. He has performed in various clubs and festivals in Amsterdam and has been associated with the Dutch electronic music scene since the 1990s.\nPerforms as: Van Bellen\nTheir channels, stations, shows, clubs, labels, collaborators: RoXY Amsterdam; Holland Festival; 3voor12; Legendary DJ Sets; Classic DJ Sets; MARY GO WILD; TM Radio; FRISKY Radio; Powapete; Classic Windsurf Movies; Windsurf Podcast; Van Bellen; Joost van Bellen\nOther people with the name (not this artist): Paul van Bellen - A windsurfer and content creator, known for his classic windsurf movies and podcasts.; Van Bellen - A DJ and producer, known for his electronic music sets and collaborations in the Dutch electronic music scene."
},
